{
    "chapter_num": 24,
    "verses_count": 27,
    "paragraphs_list": [
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Accused of Sedition"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 1,
                    "num_str": "1",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Now after five days Ananias the high priest came down with the elders and a certain orator "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "named"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " Tertullus. These gave evidence to the governor against Paul."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 2,
                    "num_str": "2",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And when he was called upon, Tertullus began his accusation, saying: “Seeing that through you we enjoy great peace, and "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Or reforms are"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "prosperity is being brought to this nation by your foresight, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 3,
                    "num_str": "3",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "we accept "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "it"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " always and in all places, most noble Felix, with all thankfulness. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 4,
                    "num_str": "4",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Nevertheless, not to be tedious to you any further, I beg you to hear, by your "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "graciousness"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "courtesy, a few words from us. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 5,
                    "num_str": "5",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "For we have found this man a plague, a creator of dissension among all the Jews throughout the world, and a ringleader of the sect of the Nazarenes. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 6,
                    "num_str": "6",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "He even tried to profane the temple, and we seized him, "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "NU ends the sentence here and omits the rest of v. 6, all of v. 7, and the first clause of v. 8."
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "and wanted to judge him according to our law. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 7,
                    "num_str": "7",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But the commander Lysias came by and with great violence took "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "him"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " out of our hands, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 8,
                    "num_str": "8",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "commanding his accusers to come to you. By examining him yourself you may ascertain all these things of which we accuse him.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 9,
                    "num_str": "9",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And the Jews also "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "NU, M joined the attack"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "assented, maintaining that these things were so."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "The Defense Before Felix"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 10,
                    "num_str": "10",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then Paul, after the governor had nodded to him to speak, answered: “Inasmuch as I know that you have been for many years a judge of this nation, I do the more cheerfully answer for myself, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 11,
                    "num_str": "11",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "because you may ascertain that it is no more than twelve days since I went up to Jerusalem to worship. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 12,
                    "num_str": "12",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And they neither found me in the temple disputing with anyone nor inciting the crowd, either in the synagogues or in the city. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 13,
                    "num_str": "13",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Nor can they prove the things of which they now accuse me. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 14,
                    "num_str": "14",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But this I confess to you, that according to the Way which they call a sect, so I worship the God of my fathers, believing all things which are written in the Law and in the Prophets. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 15,
                    "num_str": "15",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "I have hope in God, which they themselves also accept, that there will be a resurrection "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "NU omits of the dead"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "of "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "the"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " dead, both of "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "the"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " just and "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "the"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " unjust. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 16,
                    "num_str": "16",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "This "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "being"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " so, I myself always strive to have a conscience without offense toward God and men."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 17,
                    "num_str": "17",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "“Now after many years I came to bring alms and offerings to my nation, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 18,
                    "num_str": "18",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "in the midst of which some Jews from Asia found me purified in the temple, neither with a mob nor with tumult. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 19,
                    "num_str": "19",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "They ought to have been here before you to object if they had anything against me. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 20,
                    "num_str": "20",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Or else let those who are "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "here"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " themselves say "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "NU, M what wrongdoing they found"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "if they found any wrongdoing in me while I stood before the council, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 21,
                    "num_str": "21",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "unless "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "it is"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " for this one statement which I cried out, standing among them, ‘Concerning the resurrection of the dead I am being judged by you this day.’ ”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Felix Procrastinates"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 22,
                    "num_str": "22",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But when Felix heard these things, having more accurate knowledge of "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "the"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " Way, he adjourned the proceedings and said, “When Lysias the commander comes down, I will make a decision on your case.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 23,
                    "num_str": "23",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "So he commanded the centurion to keep Paul and to let "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "him"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " have liberty, and told him not to forbid any of his friends to provide for or visit him."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 24,
                    "num_str": "24",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And after some days, when Felix came with his wife Drusilla, who was Jewish, he sent for Paul and heard him concerning the faith in Christ. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 25,
                    "num_str": "25",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Now as he reasoned about righteousness, self-control, and the judgment to come, Felix was afraid and answered, “Go away for now; when I have a convenient time I will call for you.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 26,
                    "num_str": "26",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Meanwhile he also hoped that money would be given him by Paul, "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "NU omits that he might release him"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "that he might release him. Therefore he sent for him more often and conversed with him."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 27,
                    "num_str": "27",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But after two years Porcius Festus succeeded Felix; and Felix, wanting to do the Jews a favor, left Paul bound."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}